# Lightbase Edge 0.1.8 bridge — asset-layer security headers (zero CF Workers)
# BismiLLAH (0.1.8 — no X-Frame-Options at the asset layer): the shell IS the
# first document of every bridge-served page, including EMBEDDABLE ones — the
# fleet's inline-checkout pattern (e.g. KaatibAI framing BirrPay's /pay/<token>
# widget) loads the shell inside a cross-origin iframe, and a static
# X-Frame-Options: DENY here kills the widget before the service worker can
# take over (live battle-test catch 2026-10-11). Frame policy belongs to the
# SSR plane, which already sets its own per-path headers after the SW bridge.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
